  "notes": "Rabigh Refining and Petrochemical Company (Petro Rabigh; ticker 2380) audited financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/418_0_2026-03-12...). Auditor PwC. Board of Directors approved and authorized issue on Ramadan 20, 1447H / 9 March 2026. Petro Rabigh is a refining + petrochemical joint venture of Saudi Aramco and Sumitomo Chemical with no subsidiaries - these are standalone (not consolidated) statements, no non-controlling interest. The five primary statements (printed pages 6-10) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.6x); the notes are digital text. Amounts are in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). The FY2024 comparatives are restated (see the issuer's Note 26). FINANCIAL DISTRESS / GOING CONCERN: the statements are prepared on a going-concern basis with disclosure - Petro Rabigh reported a net loss of SAR 3,898.7m (2024 restated: SAR 4,544.5m loss), accumulated losses of SAR 9,190.7m, gross LOSS of SAR 1,755.3m (cost of revenue exceeded revenue) and current liabilities exceed current assets by ~SAR 13.7bn; it completed a SAR 5,263.65m Class B rights issue to founding shareholders (Aramco / Sumitomo) during the year. net_income, operating_income, gross_profit and comprehensive_income are all negative for both years; FY2025 EPS is -2.33. income_taxes_and_zakat sums the reported 'Zakat' and 'Tax' lines (also carried split); FY2024's Tax line is a +SAR 203.3m credit (deferred tax) so the net FY2024 figure is a +SAR 201.5m credit - the effective-tax plausibility bound warns for both years (a small zakat charge against a large loss, and a net credit) - expected. operating_income is the reported 'Operating loss'. other_reserves combines the statutory reserve and the negative 'Employees' share ownership plan' reserve. long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current 'Loans and borrowings' and its current portion (Petro Rabigh carries very large project debt to Aramco / PIF / banks and refinances continuously - it drew SAR 25.9bn and repaid SAR 29.5bn in 2025). IFRS 16 lease liabilities (the large gas / feedstock supply arrangements with Aramco) are mapped separately. defined_benefit_obligation is the non-current 'Employees' benefits'. deferred_tax_assets is the 'Deferred tax asset'. depreciation_amortization sums 'Depreciation' and 'Amortization' from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Payments for purchase of property, plant and equipment'. interest_paid is 'Interest paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'. No dividend. The cash-flow statement reconciles with no separate foreign-exchange effect line. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: profit or loss 6, comprehensive income 7, financial position 8, changes in equity 9, cash flows 10.",
